    description: "WHAT.\n1. A PEP 621 [project].dependencies entry zope.interface yields a node named zope. Fixing it moves that node's stable id (v15 material). The tables added in PR #2198 keep the whole name, so one package is named differently across tables of one manifest.\n2. profile.py::_parse_pyproject_deps (framework detection) reads pyproject by itself and misses [build-system], PDM, uv and Hatch tables.\n3. optional = true inside a Poetry LIST of constraints reads as runtime.\n4. The group or extra name is not in meta (needs a registered meta key).\n5. Unread: [tool.pixi.*] (conda ecosystem question), Pipfile, hatch.toml, legacy [tool.flit.metadata], Hatch build-hook dependencies.\n6. A comment in config-conventions.yaml says Poetry dev tables go through _extract_cargo_dependencies: false.\n7. Owner questions: optional is a new dependency_scope value; whether dev/build tables alone should open the directness manifest; supply_chain_summary counts declarations, not packages (poetry direct 161 -> 471 after PR #2198). Found during PR 1 of the stable-id plan, 2026-11-15 (PR #2198). Detail: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr1/STATUS.md."  # 0399
